  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \nWe propose a Fourier-based optimization approach to find a step function h that minimizes the maximum overlap C\u2085. The key insight is to leverage the convolution theorem and properties of Fourier transforms to transform the problem into the frequency domain, where certain optimizations and constraints may be more tractable. The Fourier transform of h and its complement are analyzed to derive bounds and structural properties that minimize overlap across all shifts. This approach provides a novel angle, capitalizing on harmonic analysis rather than direct combinatorial optimization.\n\n2. Mathematical specification  \n- Variables:  \n  - h \u2208 [0,1]^n with \u2211h = n/2  \n  - H(\u03c9) = Fourier transform of h  \n  - C = max_k [ (h \u22c6 (1 - h))[k] * (2/n) ]  \n\n- Objective:  \n  Minimize C by optimizing the Fourier coefficients to flatten the overlap spectrum  \n\n- Constraints:  \n  1. 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1  \n  2. \u2211h = n/2  \n  3. H(\u03c9) satisfies bounds derived from overlap minimization  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \na. Initialization  \n   - Read initial_h_values if available  \n   - n = len(initial_h_values), dx = 2/n  \n   - Compute initial Fourier coefficients H(\u03c9)  \n\nb. Fourier Domain Optimization  \n   - Formulate frequency domain constraints to minimize overlap peaks  \n   - Set up a convex optimization in the Fourier space  \n   - Solve for H(\u03c9) that minimizes max overlap  \n\nc. Time Domain Reconstruction  \n   - Inverse Fourier transform to get h\u0303(x)  \n   - Project h\u0303 to [0,1] and normalize to \u2211h = n/2  \n\nd. Local Refinement  \n   - Perturb h to improve overlap using gradient descent  \n   - Ensure feasibility after each step  \n\ne. Validation  \n   - Compute C\u2085 and ensure constraints are met  \n\n4. Search choices and useful variations  \n- Convex solver: CVXPY with Mosek  \n- Perturbation magnitude: adaptive based on progress  \n- Fourier resolution: use all possible frequencies  \n\n5. Compute budget and robustness  \n- Initial transform: ~2s  \n- Convex solve: ~100s  \n- Refinement: ~100s  \n- Total: ~200s  \n\n6. Validation and return contract  \n- Ensure h \u2208 [0,1]^n and \u2211h = n/2  \n- Recompute C\u2085 directly",
